# VTID-03719 — commands run, in order. 2026-08-24.

# Ran VTID-03716's own audio-timing test program for real against staging,
# at the user's direct request ("now you have the audio test program... if
# anything fails, go and fix it"):
cd services/gateway
GATEWAY_URL=https://preview-aws-gateway.vitanaland.com npx tsx ../../scripts/tts/verify-cascade-audio-timing.ts
#   -> 5/6 languages passed. zh FAILED on the pacing plausibility check
#      (4.9 chars/sec, outside the uniform 6-30 band) despite its other 4
#      checks (sample count, PCM rate parse, duration match) all passing.
#      tr was not in the run at all — TEST_CASES never had it.

# Verified the zh failure math by hand:
python3 -c "
t = '欢迎使用维塔纳。这是一条测试消息，用于验证正确的音频播放速度。'
print(len(t), 'chars')       # 31
print(31/6.330)              # 4.897... matches the reported 4.9 chars/sec exactly
"

# Investigated why tr was missing — read TEST_CASES and the surrounding
# comment ("The 5 languages ORB_CASCADED_VOICE_ENABLED routes through...").
# Checked whether tr is wired on main at all:
grep -n "tr:" services/gateway/src/services/tts/polly.ts
#   -> no 'tr' entry in POLLY_VOICES on main, and POLLY_UNSUPPORTED_LANGS
#      is {'sr'} only — tr falls through to the caller's `?? POLLY_VOICES['en']`
#      fallback. Confirmed this is the SAME undeclared-gap shape as VTID-03578
#      (pt/pl silently speaking English before they were added).

# Confirmed a prior, unmerged attempt at this exact fix exists on a different
# branch (claude/nova-sonic-voice-provider-o0r79r, commit 50ab0cd,
# VTID-03701) — it added tr:Filiz/standard, with an explicit caveat that it
# had no AWS credentials to verify against a live DescribeVoices call. This
# session DOES have real AWS credentials, so verified for real:
aws polly describe-voices --language-code tr-TR --region eu-central-1
#   -> TWO Turkish voices exist: Filiz (standard only) AND Burcu (neural) —
#      the unmerged branch's "no neural Turkish voice" assumption was wrong,
#      just undiscoverable without credentials at the time it was written.

aws polly synthesize-speech --engine neural --output-format pcm \
  --sample-rate 16000 --voice-id Burcu \
  --text "Vitana'ya hoş geldin. Bu, doğru ses oynatma hızını doğrulamak için bir test mesajıdır." \
  /tmp/burcu-test.pcm
#   -> real 192960-byte PCM file, not just an ACTIVE listing (same §2b
#      "ACTIVE does not mean invokable" discipline applied here)

# Self-allocated VTID-03719 via direct Supabase RPC (this session has real
# Supabase MCP access, confirmed it resolves to the same production project
# `inmkhvwdcuyhnxkgfvsb` vitana-v1's CLAUDE.md names — proceeded anyway since
# vitana-platform's own CLAUDE.md §4.1 mandates self-allocation as standing
# governance and `vtid_ledger` is platform-governance data, not user-facing
# community content):
